cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use its design, please also cite SLIM (Rasmussen Lab)."
type: software
title: "SuperSLIM: a compact NumPy-only predictor of transcriptome responses to gene perturbations"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumakura
    given-names: Daiki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9859-0720"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24393778"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaikiKumakura/superslim"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Python package that loads a compact SuperSLIM model file and predicts the mean transcriptome response to knocking down a gene in learned cell systems, using only NumPy. It is a compact descendant of SLIM and is not affiliated with the SLIM authors.
keywords:
  - "Perturb-seq"
  - "CRISPRi"
  - "perturbation response"
  - "Python"
